# Keep Packagist dist archives lean.
#
# The rule: the dist carries what a consumer can call, plus the contracts that
# describe what those calls return. Everything that only ever runs from a
# monorepo checkout — the diagnostic and parity harness, its runners, its
# Node/Playwright tooling, and migration evidence — stays out.
#
# dev/ holds harness code that is deliberately mapped through autoload-dev in
# composer.json rather than the shipped autoload block, so a dist install
# cannot resolve it even by accident.
#
# docs/contracts/* stays in the dist: install-proof.php declares those schema
# files as required, and consumers exchange reports against them.
/.gitattributes export-ignore
/.gitignore export-ignore
/composer.lock export-ignore
/homeboy.json export-ignore
/dev/ export-ignore
/tests/ export-ignore
/docs/consumer-prs/ export-ignore
/tools/benchmarks/ export-ignore
/tools/content-round-trip/ export-ignore
/tools/corpus-diagnostics/ export-ignore
/tools/live-wp-parity/ export-ignore
/tools/static-parity/ export-ignore
/tools/packagist-split/ export-ignore
/tools/visual-parity/ export-ignore
